It looks like you want to update/clean your .gitignore file for a Spring Boot / Maven project so it works well with IntelliJ, VS Code, STS, NetBeans, etc.

Here is an improved and complete version you can use:

# ===============================
# Spring Boot / Maven
# ===============================
HELP.md
target/
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
!**/src/main/**/target/
!**/src/test/**/target/

# ===============================
# Maven Wrapper
# ===============================
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.properties

# ===============================
# Logs
# ===============================
*.log

# ===============================
# OS Files
# ===============================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ===============================
# STS (Spring Tool Suite)
# ===============================
.apt_generated
.classpath
.factorypath
.project
.settings/
.springBeans
.sts4-cache

# ===============================
# IntelliJ IDEA
# ===============================
.idea/
*.iws
*.iml
*.ipr
out/

# ===============================
# NetBeans
# ===============================
/nbproject/private/
/nbbuild/
/dist/
/nbdist/
/.nb-gradle/
build/
!**/src/main/**/build/
!**/src/test/**/build/

# ===============================
# VS Code
# ===============================
.vscode/

# ===============================
# Node (if React frontend exists)
# ===============================
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# ===============================
# Environment files
# ===============================
.env
.env.local
.env.*
Why this version is better
Ignores IDE files (IntelliJ, STS, VS Code, NetBeans)

Ignores build folders (target, build)

Ignores OS junk files

Supports React frontend if you use it with Spring Boot (which you often do).

Since you work with Spring Boot microservices + React, this .gitignore will work well for your project structure.

If you want, I can also show you a professional .gitignore used in production microservice projects (Spring Boot + React + Docker + Kafka). It’s much cleaner and used in real companies.




